cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Twenty Chapters, One Robot Joint Node"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pagaran
    given-names: Joseph Ambrose
    orcid: ""
abstract: >-
  A build plan for one robot joint node, taken apart into twenty chapters and
  built on a bench without a robot arm on it. Covers a proven one kilohertz
  control period, one clock shared across sensors and bus, quadrature and
  inertial sensing, a drive stage written in full for a motor that is not
  present, CAN-FD from bit timing upward, network management, an embedded
  middleware port, standard joint message types, a closed control loop with
  following error, latched safe states, update over the bus, and a rig that
  asserts on motion quality. Three capabilities the bench cannot demonstrate are
  named and designed around rather than omitted, and every figure marks what is
  real, what is modelled and what is absent.
keywords:
  - embedded firmware
  - robotics
  - CAN-FD
  - real-time control
  - functional safety
  - STM32H7A3
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ambrosiobing/robot-joint-node"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
